course: dictionary
lesson: 6610
title: Normally: usual and ordinary
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word normally has two meanings. The first is usually, in most cases: «I normally walk to school.» The second is in a normal or ordinary way: «Breathe normally.»
explain: Use the clues around the word to decide which meaning fits. «I normally go to bed at eight» tells you that bedtime is what happens most nights. Ask yourself: would usually fit here? If it does, you have found the meaning.
explain: Stories often use normally to set up a surprise. «Normally the house was quiet, but that night…» The word tells you what usual looked like, so the next part feels strange and makes you want to read on.
fact: Normally means usually, or in a normal way.
fact: «Normally» tells you what is typical or what usually happens.
fact: Similar words are usually, generally and typically.
fact: «Normal» is an adjective, and «normally» is the adverb that comes from it.
fact: Writers use «normally» to show a routine, and then they often change it to make a story more exciting.
exercise: «I normally walk to school.» What does normally mean here? | *Usually, in most cases | Very slowly | Once only, never again | Angrily
exercise: «Breathe normally.» What does normally mean here? | Quietly, on tiptoe | Holding your breath until you go red | Loudly and fast | *In a normal, ordinary way
exercise: Which word has about the same meaning as normally? | Quickest | Angry | *Usually | Yesterday
test: «Normally the house was quiet, but that night there was a loud bang.» What does normally tell you? | *What usually happens, so the bang is surprising | It means at night | The house was always loud | Normally means never
test: Which word could replace normally in «The bus normally arrives at eight»? | *Usually | Rarely | Angrily | Suddenly
exam: Mia says normally means very quickly because it ends in -ly. Why is she wrong? | *Normally means usually or in a normal way, not quickly | Normally means very loudly | Normally means quickly, because it ends in -ly | Normally means never
